      "fragment_index": 2,
      "start": 85.3,
      "end": 173.35,
      "duration": 88.05,
      "text": "And so in the years ahead our reaction to AI will not be so much about the machine itself, it will be about our own moral conditioning. As AI agents become more integrated into our lives, we must ask what happens to our understanding of intimacy, empathy and community when human-like technology becomes embedded in our already complicated social arrangements? What happens when artificial relationships feel easier, safer and more available than human ones? Let me offer two imperatives for our collective reflection and action. First, as we deploy AI technology for efficiency and economic advancement, we must ensure this does not come at the cost of human worth or the sustainability of our species.",
