      "fragment_index": 3,
      "start": 173.35,
      "end": 263.73,
      "duration": 90.38,
      "text": "This is where the principle of human dignity must be most fiercely protected. It requires openness, inclusivity and enlightened access. People from all walks of life must have a say in the shaping of the future of AI. Second, we must teach moral literacy alongside digital media and information literacy. It's simply not good enough to show children and adults how to use artificial intelligence or to talk about the opportunities or the risks of artificial intelligence. No, that's not good enough. We must equally ensure that we help people to engage with artificial intelligence in ways that preserve their sense of self. As you explore the more than 60 video presentations at your own pace in your own time zone, let us remember that AI access in focus is not just our theme.",
